---
import { getEntry } from 'astro:content';
import Landing from '../layouts/Landing.astro';
import FoveationExplorer from '../components/FoveationExplorer.astro';
import Results from '../components/Results.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const roadmap = await getEntry('docs', 'docs/roadmap');
const upcoming = (roadmap?.data.items ?? []).filter((i) => i.status !== 'shipping').slice(0, 4);
const statusLabel: Record<string, string> = { building: 'Being built', planned: 'Planned', exploring: 'Exploring' };
---
<Landing
  title="Foveate: put the right pages in the window, and prove the answer"
  description="A Python library for long documents and agents. It picks the pages that matter, keeps the rest as an outline, and checks every citation against the source."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Context engineering for LLM apps</p>
        <h1>Put the right pages in the window. Prove the answer.</h1>
        <p class="lede">Foveate is a Python library for long documents and agents. It picks the pages that matter, keeps the rest as a short outline, and checks every citation in the answer against the page it names.</p>
        <div class="cta">
          <a class="btn primary" href={`${base}docs/quickstart/`}>Get started</a>
          <a class="btn" href={`${base}docs/`}>Read the docs</a>
        </div>
        <div class="install"><code>pip install "foveate[pdf]"</code><button type="button" data-copy='pip install "foveate[pdf]"' aria-label="Copy install command">Copy</button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="demo" aria-label="Example">
<pre class="code"><span class="k">from</span> foveate <span class="k">import</span> Document, Foveator, Runtime

document = Document.load(<span class="s">"3M_2018_10K.pdf"</span>)
question = <span class="s">"What was 2018 capital expenditure?"</span>
<span class="k">with</span> Runtime.from_env() <span class="k">as</span> runtime:
    answer = Foveator(runtime).ask(question, [document])

answer.text      <span class="c"># "$1,577 million"</span>
answer.pages     <span class="c"># [("3M_2018_10K", 60)]</span>
answer.grounded  <span class="c"># True: the quote is on page 60</span></pre>
        <p class="muted small">From a real run on the 160-page 3M 2018 annual report. If the filing did not contain the answer you would get <code>answer.abstained == True</code>, not a guess.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">The problem</p>
        <h2>What happens when you upload 200 pages</h2>
        <p>There are three common outcomes. Only the third gives you something you can check.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Send everything</h3><p class="muted">If the file is larger than the model window it fails or is silently cut. If it fits, every question costs 100,000 tokens or more, and models use the middle of a long prompt worst.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Add plain retrieval</h3><p class="muted">Cheaper, but the model gets loose chunks with no page numbers. Nothing checks the answer, and a question the file cannot answer still gets an answer.</p></article>
        <article class="card accent"><h3>Foveate</h3><p class="muted">The relevant pages arrive in full, their neighbours condensed, the rest as a one-line outline. The answer carries page citations, each quote is checked, and a missing answer is reported as missing.</p></article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block" id="explore">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Try it</p>
        <h2>See what the model would receive</h2>
        <p>These are real plans for three questions on real filings, computed by the library without calling a model. Change the budget and watch the pages change. The green ring marks the page that holds the answer. At small budgets it is sometimes missed; that is shown honestly.</p>
      </div>
      <FoveationExplorer />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>Four steps, each one inspectable</h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="steps">
        <li><h3>Load</h3><p class="muted">PDF, DOCX, HTML, Markdown or text becomes pages with numbers, headings and token counts. <code>document.select("10-14,40")</code> returns just those pages.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Select</h3><p class="muted">BM25 ranks pages with no extra dependencies. Add embeddings or a model re-rank if you want. <code>Foveator.plan()</code> shows the result and its cost before any call.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Foveate</h3><p class="muted">Best pages go in full, neighbours are condensed, everything else is an outline line, all inside the token budget you set.</p></li>
        <li><h3>Answer and verify</h3><p class="muted">The model answers in JSON with citations. Each quote is searched for on its page. Unsupported answers are retried with feedback, then flagged or turned into "not found".</p></li>
      </ol>
      <p class="more"><a href={`${base}docs/concepts/`}>Read the concepts</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Evidence</p>
        <h2>Measured against the alternatives</h2>
        <p>Same prompt, same citation check, four ways of choosing evidence. Real filings from FinanceBench, gold sets we built for citations, unanswerable questions, paraphrases and needles.</p>
      </div>
      <Results />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Beyond documents</p>
        <h2>The same ideas for agents</h2>
        <p>Agents fail on context in two ways: they are handed whole files, and their history and tool output keep growing.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-3">
        <article class="card"><h3>Page tools</h3><p class="muted"><code>read_pages</code>, <code>search_document</code> and <code>document_outline</code> for Pydantic AI, Google ADK and LangGraph. The agent pulls pages when it needs them.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>History compression</h3><p class="muted">Keep the latest turns verbatim and compress the rest to a budget, without splitting a tool call from its result.</p></article>
        <article class="card"><h3>Tool-output reducers</h3><p class="muted">JSON, CSV, HTML and logs shrink with no model call, and say what was cut ("481 more items").</p></article>
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a href={`${base}docs/guides/agents-and-tools/`}>Agents and tools guide</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Works with</p>
        <h2>Bring your own model and framework</h2>
        <p>Any provider through LiteLLM, any OpenAI-compatible server (vLLM, Ollama, NVIDIA and others), or an in-process vLLM engine. Tested on Linux, macOS and Windows with Python 3.10 to 3.13. Retries, circuit breaker, caching and OpenTelemetry spans are built in.</p>
      </div>
      <ul class="logos">
        <li>Pydantic AI</li><li>Google ADK</li><li>LangGraph</li><li>LiteLLM</li><li>OpenAI-compatible</li><li>vLLM</li><li>OpenTelemetry</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Coming next</p>
        <h2>What we are building</h2>
        <p>Position-aware prompts, query-aware condensing, long-term memory and two new benchmarks are on the list.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        {upcoming.map((item) => (
          <article class="card">
            <span class={`chip ${item.status}`}>{statusLabel[item.status]}</span>
            <h3>{item.title}</h3>
            <p class="muted">{item.summary}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p class="more"><a href={`${base}roadmap/`}>See the full roadmap</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="block final">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Start with a dry run</h2>
      <p class="lede">Plan a question on your own file without calling a model. Then ask it with citations.</p>
      <div class="cta"><a class="btn primary" href={`${base}docs/quickstart/`}>Open the quickstart</a><a class="btn" href="https://github.com/sachncs/context">View on GitHub</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-copy]').forEach((button) => {
      button.addEventListener('click', async () => {
        try {
          await navigator.clipboard.writeText(button.dataset.copy ?? '');
          button.textContent = 'Copied';
          setTimeout(() => (button.textContent = 'Copy'), 1800);
        } catch {
          button.textContent = 'Press Ctrl+C';
        }
      });
    });
  </script>
</Landing>

<style>
  .hero { padding-block: clamp(3rem, 8vw, 6rem) clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 5rem); }
  .hero-grid { display: grid; gap: var(--space-12); grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; }
  @media (min-width: 62rem) { .hero-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.05fr) minmax(0, 1fr); } }
  .cta { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-8); }
  .install { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: var(--space-3); margin-top: var(--space-6); padding: .5rem .5rem .5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; background: var(--surface); max-width: 100%; }
  .install code { font-size: .88rem; overflow-x: auto; white-space: nowrap; }
  .install button { border: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface-2); color: var(--text); border-radius: 8px; padding: .4rem .8rem; font: inherit; font-size: .85rem; cursor: pointer; min-height: 36px; }
  .demo .small { font-size: .88rem; margin-top: var(--space-3); }
  .card.accent { border-color: var(--accent); background: var(--accent-soft); }
  .steps { list-style: none; counter-reset: s; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--space-4); grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(15rem, 1fr)); }
  .steps li { counter-increment: s; padding: var(--space-6); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: var(--radius); background: var(--surface); }
  .steps li::before { content: counter(s); display: inline-grid; place-items: center; width: 2rem; height: 2rem; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: var(--on-accent); font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
  .steps p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .more { margin-top: var(--space-6); }
  .logos { list-style: none; display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: var(--space-3); padding: 0; margin: 0; }
  .logos li { padding: .5rem 1rem; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 999px; background: var(--surface); font-weight: 550; font-size: .95rem; }
  .final { text-align: center; }
  .final .lede { margin-inline: auto; }
  .final .cta { justify-content: center; }
  .card p { margin-top: var(--space-2); }
  .card .chip { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
</style>
